= Goals
The goal of this project is to create a small scale open-source alternative to certain web services using repurposed technology. With this service, it should be set up in such a way where anyone can sign into a dashboard and set up docker containers (possibly even interpreters or environments), and the task will be properly assigned to a machine that can afford the work load. \

It is critically important that the entire time we maintain an open-source and transparent nature, as well as minimize the cost of the cluster while still providing a valid alternative (learning) environment to enterprise grade linux. \

While we want this project to provide legitment competition to certain cloud providers for small-scale projects and tasks for students. First and foremost we are here to learn, and regardless of success it is imperitive that this project remains as an oppertunity to learn about the usage of linux in cloud, and distributed computing using free and open source software (FOSS) tools. 

